# descent-vk railgun: the brute's shoulder cannon. A robot attachment, not a
# robot: RobotDef::railgunModel names it, and it is drawn, shadowed and hit on
# its own so that it can be shot off.
# THIS MESH MUST STAY CLOSED. Every edge is shared by exactly two triangles.
# It is five closed boxes - receiver, power pack, barrel and two coils - which
# overlap without sharing a vertex; disjoint closed shells satisfy the rule and
# their shadow volumes overlap, which depth-fail counts correctly.
#
# Modelled about its own origin, which RobotDef::railgunMount places in the
# robot's space. -Z is forward and the muzzle is at z = -2.5. Its bounds are
# its hitbox: see resolveRobotAttachments. Wound counter-clockwise seen from
# outside; normals are not authored, the loader computes flat per-face normals.

# receiver
v   -0.500   -0.450    0.300
v    0.500   -0.450    0.300
v    0.500    0.450    0.300
v   -0.500    0.450    0.300
v   -0.500   -0.450    2.500
v    0.500   -0.450    2.500
v    0.500    0.450    2.500
v   -0.500    0.450    2.500
# power pack
v   -0.300    0.400    0.800
v    0.300    0.400    0.800
v    0.300    0.700    0.800
v   -0.300    0.700    0.800
v   -0.300    0.400    2.100
v    0.300    0.400    2.100
v    0.300    0.700    2.100
v   -0.300    0.700    2.100
# barrel
v   -0.200   -0.200   -2.500
v    0.200   -0.200   -2.500
v    0.200    0.200   -2.500
v   -0.200    0.200   -2.500
v   -0.200   -0.200    0.400
v    0.200   -0.200    0.400
v    0.200    0.200    0.400
v   -0.200    0.200    0.400
# rear coil
v   -0.320   -0.320   -1.200
v    0.320   -0.320   -1.200
v    0.320    0.320   -1.200
v   -0.320    0.320   -1.200
v   -0.320   -0.320   -0.900
v    0.320   -0.320   -0.900
v    0.320    0.320   -0.900
v   -0.320    0.320   -0.900
# front coil
v   -0.320   -0.320   -2.100
v    0.320   -0.320   -2.100
v    0.320    0.320   -2.100
v   -0.320    0.320   -2.100
v   -0.320   -0.320   -1.800
v    0.320   -0.320   -1.800
v    0.320    0.320   -1.800
v   -0.320    0.320   -1.800

vt 0.00 0.00
vt 1.00 0.00
vt 1.00 1.00
vt 0.00 1.00

